   Setup — this machine's logins, then each folder of the workspace

   ❌ gh is not logged in to github.com
      gh auth login --hostname github.com · it needs you at the keyboard
   ❌ kit check finds 2 differences from the release
      read: kit help check

   This step checks what the work in a repository needs. On this machine, it checks the command-line tool of each code
   forge your repositories use, and your login there. Then it checks each folder of the workspace on its own, the desk
   first and then each worktree. In a folder, it checks kit and the files it places, the git hooks, the tools and
   linters, and kit check.

   When a check fails, the line under it gives the command that fixes it, or says where to read more. Run the command
   yourself, or have kit run it and check again. kit runs nothing until you ask. A folder's fix runs in that folder.

   A check drawn 💡 is an offer: it holds, and you can leave it. Outside a repository, with no workspace, only the
   machine is checked. For how kit finds the folders, read docs/workspaces.md
   (https://github.com/empowerite/kit/blob/main/docs/workspaces.md).

   kit welcome --checks















